From 262e8869a72835d4bb770b7b75721755357bc84a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:15:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 889/913] drivers: stm32_exti: check the TDCID state read
 result
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

stm32_exti_rif_save called stm32_rifsc_check_tdcid without checking its
result. On error the boolean is left untouched, so the function silently
behaved as if the core were not TDCID and skipped saving the RIF
configuration, which would then be restored from a stale cache.

Panic on error as the function cannot report it to its caller.

Coverity issue: CID 1200429: Unchecked return value in stm32_exti_rif_save

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 5de5a4fec6fc05633bbce7aa3949ca44a76bf01e drivers: stm32_exti: check the TDCID state read result]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I54f2b19a57f2a64da262c03aae63db327ddd144c
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/597010
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_exti.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c b/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c
index 4ef5706b1..55e7b821b 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c
@@ -553,7 +553,9 @@ static void stm32_exti_rif_save(struct stm32_exti_pdata *exti)
 			io_read32(exti->base + _EXTI_SECCFGR(i));
 	}
 
-	stm32_rifsc_check_tdcid(&is_tdcid);
+	if (stm32_rifsc_check_tdcid(&is_tdcid))
+		panic();
+
 	if (!is_tdcid)
 		return;
 
-- 
